            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0120" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg18"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee (Arms)/99:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Delegate</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-21T13:00:00+01:00">February 21,
                            1935—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 21—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>985. Supplementing my 984, February 20, 6 p.m., paragraph 2, I suggest
                    consideration of article 33 of the 1925 Arms Traffic Convention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
